    {
      "name": "Crack Bones",
      "actions": 1,
      "traits": [],
      "description": "<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The majungasaurus has a creature Grabbed in its jaws</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The majungasaurus deals that creature <span class=\"roll\" onclick=\"roll(this)\">3d8</span> bludgeoning damage (DC 24 basic Fortitude save). A creature that fails this save is Clumsy 1 until it recovers to full Hit Points.</p>",
      "collapsed": false
    }
  ],
  "spellcastingEntries": [],
  "description": "<p>The majungasaurus prowls in a crouched posture, carrying its bulk so low to the ground it is eye-to-eye with its prey. Unlike most carnivorous dinosaurs, the majungasaurus is primarily an ambush predator, patiently lying in wait for quarry to come within reach before bursting from cover with a signature cry to attack.</p>",
